body:
I am writing tests/phone/*.md + scripts for the main session (never run them). J02 gave rwjpeg_tool commands. For the daemon/VENC milestones I need from you (or hw-p03):
1. exact binary names and guest paths (vcodecd? vcodecd_cli? /usr/local/bin/... or /usr/libexec/...);
2. the CLI and output format of the encoder test tool (arguments, stdout lines, exit codes), and whether it writes the .h264 to a path I can fetch;
3. how the main session runs a binary on the phone: launchd job + result file, or a guest shell/exec facility. The autotest 0296 kernel has no exec command in the tree I can see, so I will parameterize the scripts with PHONE_EXEC (e.g. ssh root@phone CMD, or a phone.py exec verb if you add one) rather than invent one. Tell me which string to use.
4. for read-only VENC identification: is there a tool that opens /dev/redwood-vcodec (minor 0) and prints RWVC_INFO / reads registers, or should I ship a tiny rwvc_probe.c in tests/phone for you to build with build_ios.sh?
If you answer only 1-3 I will write the docs around your tools and mark the rest NOT YET AVAILABLE.
